      "code_hash": "ae01bc733cc94b994e0a5710dc959386",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The attributes of dictionaries can be accessed with the <code>keys()</code> and <code>values()</code> methods, making it easy to extract them. These methods return <code>dict_keys</code> and <code>dict_values</code> objects, respectively. While these objects resemble lists, we can't access their elements using indexing. If you'd like to use indexing on them, it's best to convert the object to a list and access the elements from there.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "fwwy",
      "code_hash": "5c63e017977f152165de03f0b81b6212",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><br></span>\n<ol start=\"7\">\n<li>Extract the key-value pairs from our <code>tree</code> dictionary in tuples, and store the values in a single list, <code>item_list</code>.</li>\n</ol></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "LJZf",
      "code_hash": "167ffa79ed54dbfa40e4d1449692506d",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
