      "id": "urSm",
      "code_hash": "0924373e0f461180ded1e7325173e601",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Here we extracted a <code>dict_items</code> object and converted it to a list. We can see that our <code>item_list</code> variable is a list of tuples with two elements each, containing the key-value pairs from our dictionary in each tuple.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The <code>dict_items</code> object shares the attributes of the <code>dict_keys</code> and <code>dict_values</code> objects, meaning that while <code>dict_items</code> objects are iterable, we cannot use an index to access their elements.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
